gy_cli_windows_arm64.zip"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-antigravity/antigravity-cli/releases/assets/691066915","id":691066915,"node_id":"RA_kwDOScoSV84pMNgj","name":"agy_cli_windows_x64.zip","label":"","uploader":{"login":"haofan","id":3281311,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODEzMTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3281311?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/haofan","html_url":"https://github.com/haofan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haofan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haofan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haofan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haofan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haofan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haofan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haofan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haofan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haofan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/zip","state":"uploaded","size":64395542,"digest":"sha256:79140f11f0fb7222a6e543c2f446904822e27ce7a39766230fffa01d95639b67","download_count":76,"created_at":"2026-10-30T05:37:33Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T05:37:37Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/google-antigravity/antigravity-cli/releases/download/1.4.11/agy_cli_windows_x64.zip"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-antigravity/antigravity-cli/tarball/1.4.11","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-antigravity/antigravity-cli/zipball/1.4.11","body":"- Added a billing model choice after you sign in with Google Cloud, so you can pick either a Gemini subscription or Pay As You Go.\n- Added `terminationBehavior` to `PreInvocation` hooks: returning `\"terminate\"` stops the turn before the model is called, for example to block a prompt that contains sensitive data, and hooks can now inject an `errorMessage` whose `userMessage` is shown to you without being sent to the model, which also makes a `-p` run exit with a non-zero code.\n- Added a `finished_reason` field to the result of `--output-format json` and `stream-json` runs that says why a turn ended early, `print_timeout` when `--print-timeout` expired and the response is partial, `interrupted` when the run was canceled such as with `Ctrl+C`, or `error` for any other failure, so scripts can tell a cut-off answer from a complete one; the field is omitted when the turn finishes normally.\n- Improved the `/plugin` Discover tab for long shelves: each shelf now shows its first 6 plugins followed by a `⋯ N more — enter to show` row, `Ctrl+E` expands or collapses the shelf under the cursor, and `[` and `]` jump to the previous or next shelf.\n- Fixed `agy plugin import claude` printing `No claude extensions found.` for plugins installed from a Claude Code marketplace: it now reads Claude Code's list of installed plugins, skipping plugins disabled in Claude Code's settings and plugins installed for a single project only, and imported plugins now keep their remote MCP servers (`\"type\": \"http\"` with `url` and `headers`) and servers from `.mcp.json` files without an `mcpServers` wrapper, expand `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` to the installed plugin's directory, and list servers that can't be converted, such as ones using the legacy SSE transport, with a warning instead of reporting them as installed.\n"}